1
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,606
We made it here in good time.

2
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,357
Master Catviper's a pretty
sharp navigator, isn't he?

3
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,817
Though I do suppose he sailed with
the King of the Pirates after all.

4
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,841
So, how long should we
wait at these ruins anyway?

5
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,577
I feel like it's been a while.

6
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:25,097
Until Master Catviper brings
Marco the Phoenix here, of course.

7
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,010
Yeah?

8
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:26,923
You think he'll do it?

9
00:00:27,006 --> 00:00:27,836
I don't know.

10
00:00:27,919 --> 00:00:30,448
I sure hope Marco comes
with us to the land.

11
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,777
of Wano the Phoenix would make
for a pretty powerful ally.

12
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:38,557
I mean this guy is the former first
edition commander of the infamous

13
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,037
Whitebeard Pirates so he's definitely
worth the effort of coming out here.

14
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,797
I was surprised to find out he's
one of Master Cat Vipers friends.

15
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:46,710
Good point.

16
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,317
If this Marco's such a celebrity then
I want to get a good look at him.

17
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,230
Whoa wait!

18
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:55,164
Let me remind you of something.

19
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:58,837
Master said to stay put because
of your intimidating looks.

20
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:02,391
Is Marco the kind of guy who
will get scared off by a face?

21
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,300
Listen here.

22
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:08,417
He was referring to that quaint little
village of peace-loving folks up there,

23
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,382
you Karoo fool.

24
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:12,696
Big, pearly warriors like
us will frighten the locals.

25
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:13,760
I see.

26
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:18,022
But Master Cadvipers' features are
scarier than mine, I would say.

27
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,300
Like when he's mad?

28
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,677
Yeah, but he does have a cute smile.

29
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:22,590
Too true.

30
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:41,760
There! Hey, wait!

31
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:06,240
Okay, he's all fixed up now.

32
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:07,579
You're good to go.

33
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:11,217
He said you're all better now.

34
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,580
Tama, feel good?

35
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,340
Don't push yourself too hard.

36
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:24,307
The flames of restoration only
have a slight effect on others.

37
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,037
Since I patched you up your natural
healing speed will be faster now.

38
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,296
You'll be bouncing around by tomorrow

39
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,677
It feels like you're back to normal.

40
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:55,590
Oh, boy!

41
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:00,940
Take it easy.

42
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,060
Set by tomorrow.

43
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,765
Thank you for the help, Marco!

44
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,080
We love you!

45
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:15,940
Marco? Excuse me.

46
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:17,677
I got a knot in my shoulder.

47
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:19,377
Marco, I saw a knot through the mouth.

48
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:20,737
Marco, the vest was an ideal.

49
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:22,037
Could you use some tears?

50
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,179
Marco, I slipped a disc in my back.

51
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,700
All right, all right.

52
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:34,964
I'll help you all, but
one at a time now, please

53
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:55,740
Pops built this village, you know.

54
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:58,939
So he took care of the people here?

55
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,846
Is that what you got, I mean?

56
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:06,337
Countries that are too poor to pay
heavenly tribute to the Celestial

57
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,949
Dragons are not allowed to join
the world government at all.

58
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:14,580
They tend to be lawless lands where
pirates and kidnappers run amok.

59
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,607
There's no one to stop them.

60
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,077
And when the country succumbs to collapse,

61
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,780
it turns out a fresh
generation of orphans.

62
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,108
Pops was one of those kids.

63
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:32,860
With nothing left to lose, he
went out to sea at an early age.

64
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,733
Even after becoming a pirate,
he cared about this island.

65
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:45,937
He'd funneled dirty money and
supplies here whenever he could,

66
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,961
but he never revealed who he was.

67
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:49,880
Did it till he died.

68
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:55,800
He never had a family, and his
friends were all long gone.

69
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,480
But this island was always home to him.

70
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:04,382
In a corrupt world, there's no
such thing as clean or dirty money.

71
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,441
It's just money.

72
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,860
Nice of you to say.

73
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,960
So after the war in Marineford,

74
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:18,731
at the very least we wanted to protect
this village that Pops loved so much.

75
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:21,597
That's why we started
a grudge war with Teach

76
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:24,680
when he tried to invade
our territory and claim it.

77
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:29,058
But we were no match for Teach,
especially after he stole Pops' power.

78
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,880
In the end, he took everything.

79
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:41,000
I wanted him to pay, and
I wanted to do it myself.

80
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,660
Poor Pops.

81
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:53,620
It's funny.

82
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,660
He was kind of a cheapskate.

83
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:06,074
He'd always mooch drinks off of others.

84
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,784
And the guy never once
offered to cover our tap.

85
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,237
And nobody said a thing
because we all knew

86
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,791
what he was doing with the money he saved.

87
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:23,581
He was sending it to the village.

88
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,880
Well, ain't that something?

89
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:33,169
So that makes this peaceful little spot
the last memento that he left behind,

90
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,290
doesn't it?

91
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,370
Yeah.

92
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:40,560
He must be grateful.

93
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:44,127
Red-haired Shanks made
sure to bury him here.

94
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:50,760
By the way, have you heard
of a warlord named Weevil?

95
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:53,217
He said he's Pops' biological son,

96
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:56,476
and now he's attacking people
connected to Whitebeard.

97
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,420
Wow, is her claim true?

98
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,033
I'm not sure, honestly.

99
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,185
Never knew his taste in women.

100
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,977
But if I had to guess,
they're after his fortune.

101
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:08,472
And I doubt they'd believe us
if we said there wasn't one.

102
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,120
And you know what?

103
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,090
It's a shame.

104
00:07:12,173 --> 00:07:14,837
It's only a matter of time
before they come for this place.

105
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:18,280
I see that means you got our stuck here

106
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:25,049
Weevil's mother buckin was a
pirate back in her younger days

107
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:28,917
If I recall correctly, it must
have been about 30 or 40 years ago.

108
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,353
I even heard she used to be
on the very same ship as pops

109
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:38,520
And maybe you gotta have another
memento of his to protect

110
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,586
Not sure about that,
considering his behavior.

111
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:44,880
A fine pint!

112
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:54,249
If you're going to see Straw Hat Luffy
after this, can you pass on a message?

113
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:55,350
Nothing big.

114
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,260
Yeah, not a problem.

115
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,480
You said you're going to Wano? Yep.

116
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,900
Luffy, it says the referee kicked off.

117
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:12,177
Royalty from all over are attending.

118
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,201
They're at the conference
in Marie Joie right now.

119
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,637
All eyes are on a set
of guests who haven't

120
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:22,940
participated in two centuries
through a Yuku kingdom.

121
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:26,693
King Neptune will be in
attendance with all his children.

122
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,470
Ha!

123
00:08:28,553 --> 00:08:31,121
Seems like Shirahoshi was
a big hit with everyone.

124
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:34,377
That means she went up
to the surface, huh?

125
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:35,754
She's getting tougher.

126
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:36,960
I'm proud of her.

127
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:42,693
It says here that your grandpa
was their personal escort.

128
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:47,297
Sounds like they're making arrangements
to relocate fishmen to the land.

129
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:48,909
Their dream's coming true.

130
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,510
Huh?

131
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,440
Vivi, my sweet!

132
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:58,909
You're even more
beautiful than I remember.

133
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,491
I just want to smooch ya.

134
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:01,930
What's that?

135
00:09:02,013 --> 00:09:02,960
You want another?

136
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,257
Oh, do I get some change back?

137
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:06,520
Let me get in close.

138
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:08,780
Knock it off!

139
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,590
Vivi!

140
00:09:13,673 --> 00:09:14,600
It's really her.

141
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,160
Wow, that's awesome.

142
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,677
It's been a while.

143
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,320
She looks so elegant and formal now.

144
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:23,080
Oh, I hope I get to meet her someday.

145
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,777
Do you think Vivi might be
interested in your mere panties?

146
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:27,880
I don't think so!

147
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:34,269
Oh, these are photos
of the Mingling Plaza.

148
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,397
Look at all the royal families.

149
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,980
Tons of bodyguards, too.

150
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:41,797
People from Dressrosa should
be there as well, right?

151
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,800
There she is, Viola!

152
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,780
Ugh! Waffle!

153
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,780
Hey, an acorn guy!

154
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,900
Huh? Waffle?

155
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,001
Why is he there?

156
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,140
That's Rebecca and Psy!

157
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,948
I know a lot of these guys!

158
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:03,410
No kidding.

159
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:07,017
Though I suppose any royalty we
know would be at the reverie.

160
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,571
That's kind of the point.

161
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,680
If that's the case,

162
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,717
then just maybe all the
princesses I've ever

163
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,257
met are in this same
place at the same time.

164
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:21,440
I bet they're all getting
excited talking about me.

165
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,365
You keep thinking that, buddy.

166
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,100
Chopper, look. Did you see?

167
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,280
Right there.

168
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:35,060
Chill, bro. What's going on?

169
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:44,980
It's Dr. Reed!

170
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,800
Ugh, the old bag's still alive.

171
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,130
Dr. Reed!

172
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:00,120
Hey, don't cut up the paper!

173
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:03,000
I wanted to save it, Chopper! Whoa!

174
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,317
Give me the section with the princesses.

175
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:06,920
What are you two doing?

176
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:14,740
You morons!

177
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,497
I wasn't finished reading it yet!

178
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:18,168
It's all full of holes now!

179
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,500
Oh, an article about Kaido?

180
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,917
And Big Mom 2?

181
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:27,920
Hang on.

182
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:31,680
Sanji, Chopper, give me
those pages back! Nuh-uh!

183
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:37,780
Glad to hear everyone's doing so good!

184
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:41,517
Once we're done sailing around
the world, let's go see them all.

185
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,071
Well, that sounds like a novel idea to me.

186
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:46,517
Anyway, back to getting things in order.

187
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,577
Have you tried to see if the
transponder snail can connect yet?

188
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:50,660
Ugh, I forgot.

189
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,380
Hey, this is Luffy.

190
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:54,880
Is anyone there?

191
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,020
No luck.

192
00:11:58,260 --> 00:11:59,260
Nobody picked up.

193
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,180
Forget it. Let's go.

194
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,480
Hang on, Luffy.

195
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,060
What's wrong now?

196
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,380
Feel that wind?

197
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,140
This can't be a good sign.

198
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,520
I've never seen waves like those.

199
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,240
And the wind here is freezing cold.

200
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,880
But I think this is the sea around Wano.

201
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:58,077
Do you all feel how the wind keeps
getting stronger the closer we get?

202
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,984
And the waves only grow taller.

203
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,641
Take notice of how it's spinning.

204
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,034
That's not just from the wind currents.

205
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,140
That's a very unusual flow.

206
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,290
Look.

207
00:13:09,373 --> 00:13:11,299
See how it's picking up over there?

208
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,420
I believe we should avoid the storm.

209
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,617
Maybe buy ourselves a little time?

210
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,417
What are you talking about, Brooke?

211
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,917
Don't worry about that junk.

212
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Let's keep going.

213
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:33,944
But Luffy, why would you deliberately put
your crew in such a dangerous situation?

214
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:35,700
I don't know.

215
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,058
I think he's right.

216
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,440
When we left, Kin'emon did
give me a heads-up about this.

217
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,580
I'll explain it on the
auditory snail apparatus.

218
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:50,977
As you approach the land of Wano, you'll
find the entrance to be quite perilous.

219
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:54,420
The weather grueling, the
tides violently churning.

220
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,800
It's a difficult country to enter.

221
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:58,130
Huh?

222
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,181
The weather is always this awful?

223
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:03,217
I suppose we have no other
choice if that's the case.

224
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,737
And that's why we should just go!

225
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:08,879
There's Samurai warriors are mighty,
plus it's this hard to get into?

226
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:11,480
No wonder it's such an isolated country.

227
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,510
Hmm.

228
00:14:13,593 --> 00:14:14,842
Let me think this over a little.

229
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:17,940
There has to be some way
to get us in there safely.

230
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:19,890
Yo!

231
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:24,360
What's that thing?

232
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:25,720
It's an octopus!

233
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,100
That guy's big!

234
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,940
Why is it on the ship?

235
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:30,357
Because we're at sea!

236
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:32,160
I realized that, Carrot!

237
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:34,220
Come on board!

238
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:39,576
Hey, while you're over there bickering,
those waters are pulling us in!

239
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,320
It doesn't matter!

240
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,440
Come on, Sunny!

241
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,960
Let's go to the Land of Water!

242
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,722
Hey, it looks like
something's coming towards us!

243
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,100
Uh-oh, what is it?

244
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,657
It kind of looks like a giant fish to me!

245
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:15,377
Is it a shark? Please, no!

246
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,980
It's Viggettus!

247
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,360
Koi fish?

248
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,720
Oh, wow, cool!

249
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:34,980
He's huge!

250
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:36,490
Yo!

251
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,420
A whole school of Goy.

252
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,277
What the hell are those
things doing in the sea?

253
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,780
They're freshwater fish.

254
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:58,115
How can they survive?

255
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:59,070
Who knows?

256
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,712
They're monsters anyway.

257
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,620
Hey, Saji, do these things fry up okay?

258
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,016
That stuff's not important right now.

259
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:11,017
I guess it's possible if you wash them
in hot water and then serve them chilled.

260
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:14,377
You can make our eye or I
can simmer them in some Miss.

261
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:18,137
I can batter them up and make tempura
or simmer them in sweet sauce.

262
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:24,600
Once we find the rest of the crew
let's celebrate with one of these.

263
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,140
Hey, don't struggle!

264
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,817
Of course it's gonna struggle!

265
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:44,097
You think it's gonna just let you eat it?

266
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,060
And Sanji,

267
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:48,817
you're the one who put this dumb idea
in his head, so you go bring him back!

268
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,371
It's not that big a deal.

269
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:53,000
We know he can manage on his own. Huh?

270
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:56,208
Let's just worry about
protecting the Sonny.

271
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,740
The wind is picking up!

272
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:21,120
Carrot, probe a tail! On it!

273
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,460
I need help!

274
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:44,077
Crazy look, how clean the water is?

275
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,397
It's crystal clear,
like a mountain stream.

276
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,897
I'd rather not see.

277
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:48,917
Thank you very much.

278
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,857
The giant fish are freaking me
out—is this a river? No way!

279
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,377
It looks like they're all
headed to the same place.

280
00:17:57,460 --> 00:18:02,437
Hang on tight—we're just
along for the ride now!

281
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,350
ride now

282
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:05,648
There's movies on the road!

283
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,640
What the hell?

284
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,240
How's that possible?

285
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:23,900
The river's flowing into the waterfall,
not away from it, like usual.

286
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,460
I see.

287
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:40,057
There must be a massive freshwater
source at the top of the falls.

288
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,737
That's why it's not seawater.

289
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,660
I wonder, could that be 1-0 up there?

290
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,356
You think that's it?

291
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,186
None of this makes any sense!

292
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:50,140
I'm scared! It's terrifying!

293
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:14,160
Oh, cool!

294
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:17,540
The fish are climbing
the waterfall! They are!

295
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,860
Go Koi Fish!

296
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,000
Go Koi Fish!

297
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:31,297
I'm not sure how we can
get the Sunny up there.

298
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,037
We'll think if we take it head on.

299
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:34,885
Open to suggestions right now!

300
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:36,360
You're back!

301
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,760
Wow, you see that?

302
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,076
Those koi are tough!

303
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:42,065
You can admire the fish later!

304
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,320
Luffy, the ship's going to sink!

305
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:45,960
Right, I got this!

306
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:47,430
Huh?

307
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:51,180
You should probably hang on tight!

308
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,760
Leave the way, fish!

309
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,680
Are you kidding me?

310
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,180
Let's go!

311
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:24,560
Here we go!

312
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,640
We're doing it!

313
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:56,624
You know, I'm starting to think
Wano isn't going to be very nice.

314
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:58,133
I'm sick of this chaos.

315
00:20:58,660 --> 00:21:00,680
Guys, that's the shore over there.

316
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,680
No, not awesome!

317
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:20,320
Loopy, let go of the fish! No, never!

318
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:21,599
They're my dinner!

319
00:21:22,140 --> 00:21:23,660
I've had enough of you!

320
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,200
Ross, take the helm!

321
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,113
That's your wish, Nami!

322
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,660
No use!

323
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:42,646
The current's way too strong!

324
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:48,960
Damn it!

325
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:50,905
And we were almost there, too!

326
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:57,260
It was nice telling you!
Dr. Lean! I need it!

327
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,760
Where's my koi?

328
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,280
We're already floofy!

329
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:18,980
Oh no!

330
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:22,100
We're getting flushed!

331
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:31,630
Thank you.
